// The exe's application icon. scripts\build.ps1 compiles this into
// icon_windows_amd64.syso with windres, and go build links that .syso automatically.
//
// This file and the .ico it names live next to tools\genicon\gen_icon.py, not under build\:
// build\ is artifacts only and -Clean deletes all of it, which once took the icon's own
// sources with it and left the next build unable to restore them.
//
// windres resolves the path below relative to this file, not to the caller's cwd.
//
// ID must be 3: wails v3 loads the embedded app icon by that fixed resource ID for its
// message and task dialogs (see vendor\github.com\wailsapp\wails\v3\pkg\application\
// dialogs_windows.go, LoadIconWithResourceID(handle, 3)). Any other ID still shows up in
// Explorer, but the dialogs fall back to the system icon.
3 ICON "icon.ico"
